#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""needs-you-jira: turn changes on the Jira issues assigned to you into needs-you cards.

  needs-you-jira [--dry-run] [--verbose] [--state PATH]

Run it every ~5 minutes (cron, a systemd user timer or a LaunchAgent) on one machine. It
is opt-in: it does nothing until NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_SITE is set. Each run:

  1. A search for your issues updated since the last run (Jira Cloud: GET
     /rest/api/3/search/jql, paged with nextPageToken; Data Center 8.14+: GET
     /rest/api/2/search), with each issue's changelog, so it knows who moved it.
  2. A second search for your open issues (statusCategory != Done): an issue that was
     yours and isn't in it any more was unassigned (or left your filter).
  3. For an issue whose `updated` moved, its latest comments, to count new ones and see
     whether one mentions you. Comment bodies are read for that and never copied.
  4. A status change, new comment, mention or new assignment is diffed against the last
     run's saved state and becomes one card per issue, updated in place (the title says
     the latest event). It is re-posted every run with an expiry of 3x the interval and
     resolved when the issue reaches Done, is no longer yours, when you made the latest
     change (you've already acted), or after 24 h with nothing new.

The first run (and the first after the scope settings change) only records what's there:
installing it never posts a burst of old changes.

Everything read from Jira is untrusted: only the issue summary and status name reach a
card (cleaned, redacted, truncated); comment bodies and descriptions never do. The token
is read from a mode-600 file and never logged, printed or stored. It always exits 0.

Config (environment, else ~/.config/needs-you/env):
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_SITE        https://acme.atlassian.net, or the Data Center base URL (https only).
                             Unset: the poller does nothing.
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_AUTH        cloud | dc (default: cloud for *.atlassian.net, else dc)
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_EMAIL       your Atlassian account email (cloud only)
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_TOKEN_FILE  file holding the API token (cloud) or personal access token (dc);
                             default ~/.config/needs-you/jira-token. Must be mode 600 (or 400)
                             and yours: a file others can read is refused.
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_CA_FILE     a PEM file of the CA(s) that sign a Data Center server's certificate,
                             for a private CA. Set, only it is trusted (not the system's CAs);
                             the certificate and host name are still checked.
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_EVENTS      status,comment,assigned,mention (default all); "-mention" drops one
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_STATUSES    Blocked=urgent,In Review=normal,Backlog=off,*=low: the priority of a
                             card for an issue in that status, "off" for no status card;
                             statuses not listed get the "*" rule (no "*": no status card).
                             Unset: every status change, low.
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_PROJECTS    ACME=work:normal,OPS=work:urgent: the projects to watch (only these),
                             each one's context and base priority. Unset: every project.
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_JQL_EXTRA   more JQL, added as "AND (<it>)", so it can only narrow the search:
                             'labels != noise'. Refused if its quotes or parentheses don't balance
                             or it has ORDER BY.
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_WATCHING    1 = also issues you watch (no "assigned" cards for those)
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_INTERVAL    minutes between runs (default 5); cards expire after 3x this
  NEEDS_YOU_JIRA_MAX_CARDS   at most this many cards open at once (default 20; urgent first)
  NEEDS_YOU_BIN              path to the needs-you CLI (default: on PATH, else ~/.local/bin)

State: ~/.local/state/needs-you/jira.json (mode 600): issue keys, statuses, last comment ids,
what it posted. No token, no comment text.
Python 3.9+ standard library only.
"""
